<div class="page-header"><h1 class="page-header__title">HelloDeploy Premium</h1><p class="page-header__subtitle">Extra room for pilot projects that ship often.</p></div>
<div class="card prose"><div class="card__body">
  <h2>Not for sale</h2>
  <p>Premium is not a paid plan, and there is no way to buy it. During the pilot, an administrator can grant it to accounts that need more room, based on available server capacity.</p>
  <h2>What Premium changes</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>No monthly deployment limit</li>
    <li>Projects approved automatically once they pass every readiness check</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Memory, CPU, and other limits stay the same. Premium can be removed if capacity runs short, and it does not carry over to any future version of the service.</p>
  <h2>Ask for Premium</h2>
  <p>Email <a href="mailto:<%= legalContactEmail %>"><%= legalContactEmail %></a> with the account email you sign in with and what you are building.</p>
  <p><a href="/service-limits">Service limits</a> · <a href="/pilot">Pilot and pricing</a> · <a href="/dashboard">Back to your dashboard</a></p>
</div></div>
